    "body": "## Problem\n\nSwift lets a declaration give an argument label a separate local name, and keywords are valid labels:\n\n```swift\nfunc sample(for value: Int, enabled: Bool) -> Int { ... }\n```\n\n`SwiftReplaceLabel.preprocess` already masks `keyword:` (e.g. `run(for: x)`), but not `keyword localName:`. The `for` above was treated as a loop: for one fixture the function reported CCN 6 / cognitive 1, while the identical body with `_ value` reported CCN 5 / cognitive 8.\n\n## Change\n\nAfter `(` or `,`, when a condition keyword (or `init`/`subscript`/`deinit`) is followed by one identifier, `_`, or a backticked name and then `:`, mask it the same way the existing `keyword:` case does. Comments and newlines between the parts are skipped with the existing helper. No other parsing changes.\n\nReal loops are unaffected: a `for` statement never follows `(` or `,`, so `for i: Int in xs` is still counted.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew `Test_Swift_keyword_argument_labels` in `test/test_languages/testSwift.py`, through the public analyzer with the cognitive extension. Each asserts exact (CCN, cognitive) values:\n- `for`/`if`/`while`/`guard`/`catch`/`case` labels with a local name give the same (5, 8) as the `_ value` baseline, including as a later parameter\n- `_` and backticked local names\n- comments and newlines between label, local name and colon\n- existing call labels (`run(for: x, if: y, case: z)`) unchanged\n- real `for` loops, including a typed `for i: Int in`, still counted\n\nAll new label tests fail without the fix.\n\n## Test plan / limitations\n\nNix was not available on the machine I worked on, so I didn't run `nix develop -c make`. I used a plain venv on Python 3.14 instead:\n- `python -m pytest test/test_languages/testSwift.py`: 28 passed, 10 subtests passed\n- `python -m pytest`: 2970 passed, 7 skipped, 2 failed. The two failures (`testFilesFilter` gitignore tests) also fail on unmodified `master` in that environment, so they're unrelated to this change.\n- `pycodestyle lizard.py lizard_ext lizard_languages lizard_core`: clean\n- `pylint` on `swift.py`: no new messages\n\nI opened this as a draft so CI can run the full matrix. I didn't add a CHANGELOG entry and am happy to add one wherever you prefer.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
